---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const articles=await getCollection('articles');
const counts={Learn:articles.filter(a=>a.data.section==='Learn').length,Reference:articles.filter(a=>a.data.section==='Reference').length,Do:articles.filter(a=>a.data.section==='Do').length};
const total=articles.length;
---
<Base title="howto.email — Practical email infrastructure documentation" description="Free, vendor-neutral documentation and troubleshooting tools for SMTP, DNS, SPF, DKIM, DMARC, deliverability and email security.">
<section class="home-hero"><div class="wrap home-hero-grid"><div class="home-intro"><p class="home-overline">EMAIL INFRASTRUCTURE, WITHOUT THE HAND-WAVING</p><h1>Figure out how email <span>actually works.</span></h1><p class="lead">Notes, references, runbooks and tools for the parts of email that usually turn into a DNS lookup, a message trace, or an RFC rabbit hole.</p><div class="home-actions"><a class="primary-action" href="/tools/domain-check/">Check a domain →</a><a class="secondary-action" href="/start/">Start from the beginning</a></div><p class="home-proof">{total} articles · free · vendor neutral · open source</p></div>
<aside class="quick-panel"><p class="kicker">QUICK LOOKUP</p><h2>Already know what you need?</h2><div class="quick-links"><a href="/reference/dmarc/"><strong>DMARC</strong><span>Policy, alignment and reporting →</span></a><a href="/reference/spf/"><strong>SPF</strong><span>Mechanisms, limits and results →</span></a><a href="/reference/dkim/"><strong>DKIM</strong><span>Signing, selectors and keys →</span></a><a href="/reference/smtp/"><strong>SMTP</strong><span>Transport, commands and behavior →</span></a></div></aside></div></section>
<section class="wrap home-work"><div class="home-section-head"><p class="kicker">START WITH THE PROBLEM</p><h2>What are you trying to do?</h2></div><div class="task-grid"><a href="/troubleshoot/"><strong>Something is broken</strong><span>Start with the symptom: bounced, delayed, spam, authentication or TLS.</span></a><a href="/tools/domain-check/"><strong>Check a domain</strong><span>Inspect public MX, SPF, DKIM, DMARC, MTA-STS and TLS-RPT configuration.</span></a><a href="/start/"><strong>Learn email end to end</strong><span>Follow DNS → SMTP → authentication → TLS → deliverability → security.</span></a><a href="/standards/"><strong>Find the standard</strong><span>Map the protocol you are working with back to its RFCs and registries.</span></a></div></section>
<section class="home-library"><div class="wrap"><div class="home-section-head"><p class="kicker">THE LIBRARY</p><h2>Use the level of detail you need.</h2></div><div class="library-rows"><a href="/learn/"><span><b>Learn</b><small>{counts.Learn} guides</small></span><p>Concepts and architecture. Start here when you need the mental model before the syntax.</p><b>→</b></a><a href="/reference/"><span><b>Reference</b><small>{counts.Reference} references</small></span><p>Protocols, DNS records, headers, status codes, standards and exact terminology.</p><b>→</b></a><a href="/do/"><span><b>Do</b><small>{counts.Do} procedures</small></span><p>Runbooks for testing, deploying, migrating, monitoring and troubleshooting email.</p><b>→</b></a></div><div class="utility-links"><a href="/glossary/">Glossary →</a><a href="/topics/">Browse topics →</a><a href="/search/">Search everything →</a><a href="/tools/">Tools →</a></div></div></section>
<section class="wrap home-note"><p><strong>Why this exists.</strong> Email is old, distributed and full of implementation details that get flattened into bad advice. howto.email keeps the protocol details close to the practical work: see the record, understand what it means, read the standard, make the change, and test again. <a href="/about/">About the project →</a></p></section>
</Base>